{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"title":"Choosing what to record","anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"],"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Traffluent","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a struct, so the compiler checks its name and every property. A tracker holds back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the events the user hasn’t consented to, stamps the rest with their session and device, keeps them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on disk and delivers them to your server, sending again when the network or the server fails.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"An-apps-analytics-from-launch","level":3,"text":"An app’s analytics, from launch","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare the events. The tracker rejects an event that breaks a constraint before it is stored or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value reaches only the destinations that don’t redact it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","import TrackingPlans","","@Event(name: \"product_added_to_cart\")","struct ProductAddedToCart {","    var productID: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(1), .maximum(10))","    var quantity: Int","}","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Build the tracker and start its delivery once, as the app launches:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func startAnalytics(consent: Consent) throws -> Tracker {","    \/\/ The plan and the store each take every @Event in the app, and the library's own.","    let plan = try TrackingPlan()","    \/\/ Records wait on disk until they are delivered, across launches.","    let store = try SegmentStore()","    \/\/ Every event gets its session, and the app, device, OS, locale and network it was tracked on.","    let tracker = Tracker(","        store: store,","        consent: consent,","        enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","","    let collector = HTTPDestination(","        endpoint: collectorURL,","        headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","        encoder: CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan))","    \/\/ Analytics events only, without their email addresses, 20 at a time or every 30 seconds.","    let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","        to: collector.accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues())","    Task {","        do {","            try await delivery.execute()  \/\/ for the life of the app","        } catch {","            print(\"Delivery stopped: \\(error)\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Every event that won't arrive, and why.","    let rejections = tracker.rejectionReports","    let consentDrops = consent.dropReports","    let storeDrops = store.dropReports","    let collectorDrops = collector.dropReports","    Task {","        await withDiscardingTaskGroup { group in","            group.addTask { for await report in rejections { print(\"Rejected: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in consentDrops { print(\"Not consented: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in storeDrops { print(\"Not stored: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in collectorDrops { print(\"Not sent: \\(report)\") } }","        }","    }","    return tracker","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then make the tracker the app’s default and hand it to the views, which track through it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct StoreApp: App {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init() {","        do {","            \/\/ The user's earlier decisions, which the app saved; undecided categories wait in memory.","            let tracker = try startAnalytics(consent: Consent(savedDecisions))","            \/\/ `Tracker.current` falls back to it where nothing else reaches, such as a detached task.","            try Tracker.bootstrap(tracker)","            self.tracker = tracker","        } catch {","            print(\"Analytics are off: \\(error)\")","            tracker = .noOp","        }","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            CartView()","                .tracker(tracker)","        }","    }","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Add to Cart\") {","            tracker.track(ProductAddedToCart(productID: \"canvas-tote\", quantity: 1))","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module except "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" and the testing modules, which are products of their own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Where-to-go-next","level":3,"text":"Where to go next","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set it up step by step, from adding the package to testing what you track: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare events and their constraints: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; change one that has shipped:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Track from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit views: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"},{"type":"text","text":"; let screens, controls and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app’s lifecycle track themselves: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach the tracker from any code, batch records and add context to them: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep events when the app ends or goes offline before delivering them: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ask for consent and gate events by it: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a fraction of events or sessions: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group events into sessions and stamp them with the app and device: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A session’s key is a UUIDv7, its start time in Unix milliseconds followed by random bits, held in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"memory only."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Export the events’ schemas and catch breaking changes in CI: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Test what your code tracks: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Send to logs, traces, your own server, PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment, RudderStack,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io, Google Analytics from a server or memory, with values for one destination alone:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send to an analytics vendor not yet covered, from a module of your own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Decide what belongs in an event and what stays out of it: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"references":{"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"HeapEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/heapencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to Heap as custom events, through its server-side bulk track API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"role":"collection","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each screen."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"role":"article","title":"Tracking Events","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","type":"topic"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","title":"Changing an Event"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"role":"article","title":"Defining Events","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"role":"article","title":"Persisting Records","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"topic"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"title":"Trackers","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"title":"SwiftUITracking","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"MatomoEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"PostHogEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"title":"Checksums","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/checksums","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The CRC-32 checksum of raw bytes, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked, in order."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","title":"TrackerTesting"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"role":"article","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","abstract":[{"text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","type":"topic"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"role":"collection","title":"GRDBPersistence","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"topic"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"title":"CollectorEncoding","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to send.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"title":"TracingDestinations","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"title":"PropertyJSON","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The vendor-neutral pieces a JSON ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"text":" is built from: properties, context, timestamps, identity and batch splitting.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale and network connection it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","title":"StandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding":{"title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","abstract":[{"text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"title":"AppKitTracking","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"role":"collection","title":"Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/destinations","abstract":[{"text":"Where tracked events go: the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"topic"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"title":"SnowplowEncoding","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"role":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"role":"collection","title":"DestinationTesting","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"role":"collection","title":"UIKi